-- title:
--   Free-group representations and bounded operators are Borel bireducible
-- statement:
--   Let $H=\ell^2(\mathbb N,\mathbb C)$ and let $\mathbb F_\infty$ be the free group on countably many generators. Equip its unitary representation space with the Borel structure generated by strong pointwise evaluation, and equip the bounded operators on $H$ with the strong-operator Borel structure. Unitary equivalence on these two spaces is Borel bireducible:
--
--   $$\cong_{\operatorname{Rep}(\mathbb F_\infty,H)}\ \sim_B\ \cong_{\mathcal B(H)}.$$
--
--   The reductions use a fixed canonical Hilbert space on both sides and preserve and reflect equivalence under a single common unitary. This is the right-hand comparison in Theorem 1.6 of Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.6; source BenchmarkOperatorTransport.lean, lines 100–109; source SHA-256 114aff4f6643ef17fa6a0383fa890dcea4b125ca5a8e4ff0e94b7ab7242aa0b3. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (source commit not yet published).

